Package: arpirisk
Title: ARPI Treatment Effects by Baseline Risk in Metastatic Prostate Cancer
Version: 0.1.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Wataru", "Fukuokaya", email = "wfukuokaya@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Predicts the 4-year risk of all-cause death with androgen
    deprivation therapy alone in patients with metastatic hormone-sensitive
    prostate cancer, and estimates the treatment effects on overall survival of
    adding an androgen receptor pathway inhibitor at that risk: the difference
    in 4-year survival probability, the restricted mean survival time
    difference through 4 years, and the hazard ratio. The model was developed
    from individual participant data of 4 randomized clinical trials.
